    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "CHAMBE\nIndustry\nCommerce\nAgriculture\nAviation\nCivics\nCoffeyville, Kane\nAUTO,\nMOTORCYCLE\nAIR CIRCUS N)\nJuly 4, 1931\nCOFFEYVILLE, KANS.\nCENTRE OF S. E. KANS•\nGEYVT.\nJUL 4 r\n2 PM\nKANS\n1931\nE\ns S050\nINVOR DSV VAY UPS POSINA GA\n193\nVA AIR MAIL\nD.a anchmy\n2809 fh. femm\nSeattle wasl",
      "Beo. W. Eckhardt.\nмоуп\n1999.023.020 0)",
      "COFFEYVILLE\nKANSAS\n**%\nA PROGRESSIVE AND\nINDUSTRIOUS CITY\nPOPULATION, 22,000\nUNLIMITED SUPPLY OF\nNATURAL GAS\n[For domestic and factory fuel. Carried\ninto Coffeyville by four trunk pipelines]\nELECTRIC POWER\nPURE WATER\nCoffeyville\nChamber of Commerce\nJOURNAL PRESS",
      "TRANSPORTATION FACILITIES\nMissouri Pacific Railway.\nDivision point.\nFifty miles of track.\nand quarter million dollar payroll.\nIron Mountain Railway.\nMissouri-Kansas-Texas\nRailway\nAtchison, Topeka \u0026 Santa Fe Railway.\nUnion Traction\nConnecting with the Frisco at Cherryvale.\nBus Lines in all directions.\nCommercial Airport and School of Aviation.\nOne\nUTILITIES\nCoffeyville Municipal Light \u0026 Power Plant—\nTotal Capacity..\n7259 K. W.\nDemand...\n2000 K. W.\nReserve Capacity..\n5250 K. W.\nPower Rates (sliding\nscale),\n5C,\n3c and le\nper K.\nW.\nDomestic Rates (sliding scale), 6c, 4c and 3c\nper K. W.\nTwo miles\nwhite way, five-globe light stand-\naras illuminating\ncommercial district.\nRresidence district is lighted by\n300 watt\nlamps at practically\nevery street intersection.\nThe industrial circuit extending from the plant\nin both directions,\nforming\nvenient access to\n1oop\nwith\nall industrial plants.\nPower Transmission Line—\nSouthwestern Bell Telephone Co.-\nCoffeyville Municipal Water Works—\nSource of Water-Verdigris river.\nInpounded Supply—600,000,000 gallons.\nAverage Daily Consumption-2,500,000\ngallons.\nStorage Reservoir Capacity-8,000,000 gallons.\nDaily Pumping Capacity-1,000,000 gallons.\nDaily Filter Capacity-6,000,000\ngallons.\nAverage Hyarant Pressure\nthroughout the\nCity-66 pounds.\nForty-two Miles of Water Mains ranging in\nsize from four inches to sixteen\ninches.\n195 three-way fire\nhydrants with steamer\nconnections.\nThe City Water Supply is chemically treated;\nit is analyzed weekly and found 100 per cent\npure.\nWater\nRates are as follows:\nFirst 30,000 gal. per month—25c per\n1,000 gal.\nNext 80,000 gal. per month—20c per\n1,000\nNext 900,000\ngal.\ngal. per month-loc per 1,000 gal.\nNext 1,000,000 gal. per month-10c per 1,000 gal.\nAll additional—4½c per 1000 gallons.\n1999.023.030 C"
    ],
